--
-- Test Description
-- This test checks the operation of the RX TCP offload engine, with IP frames
-- which have flaws in them so that the checksums should not be checked.
-- This test is run in gigabit TBI FIFO mode.
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
-- * Checks that the TOE recognises that these are not proper IP, TCP or UDP 
--   frames and therefore does not validate the checksum.
-- 
-- Detailed Test Description
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts
--     and then enable receive in TBI mode into a 32-bit FIFO data bus.
--  3. Send several IP frames which have flaws in them so that the checksums
--     should not be checked.
--
-- Test 4.1
--    Broadcast frame, No VLAN, type not 0800 (ARP)
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.2
--    Broadcast frame, No VLAN, type/len = 0x0024, not SNAP (DSAP, 
--    SSAP = 0x5555).
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.3
--    Broadcast frame, No VLAN, type/len = 0x0024, not SNAP (Next 2 octets
--    not equal to 0x0300 actually 0x00C0).
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.4
--    Broadcast frame, No VLAN, type/len = 0x0024, not SNAP (Next 2 octets 
--    not equal to 0x0000).
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.5
--    Broadcast frame, No VLAN, type/len = 0x0024, SNAP but not IP (Next 
--    2 octets not equal to 0x0800).
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and SNAP (bit 24 high).
-- Test 4.6
--    Broadcast frame, VLAN tag > 4 octets.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.7
--    Broadcast frame, VLAN tag = 4 octets, type/len = 0x0806.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.8
--    Broadcast frame, VLAN tag = 4 octets, type/len = 0x0010, not SNAP.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.9
--    Broadcast frame, Not IPv4 (IPv6 flag in IP header).
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.10
--    Broadcast frame, IP header length too short.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.11
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, No VLAN or SNAP, IP and TCP checksums OK, 
--    but TOE is disabled in network config register.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.12
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, VLAN, no SNAP, IP and TCP checksums OK, 
--    but TOE is disabled in network config register.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.13
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, VLAN, SNAP, IP and TCP checksums OK, 
--    but TOE is disabled in network config register.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.14
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, No VLAN, SNAP, IP and TCP checksums OK, 
--    but TOE is disabled in network config register.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.15
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, VLAN with CFI, no SNAP, IP and TCP checksums OK.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.16
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, VLAN with CFI, SNAP, IP and TCP checksums OK.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.17
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, no VLAN, bad SNAP (DSAP OK, SSAP bad).
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.18
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, no VLAN, bad SNAP (SSAP OK, DSAP bad).
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.19
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, no VLAN, bad SNAP (CONTROL OK, ID[7:0] bad).
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.20
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, no VLAN, bad SNAP (ID[7:0] OK, CONTROL bad).
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.21
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, no VLAN, bad SNAP (ID[15:8] OK, ID[23:16] bad).
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.22
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, VLAN, SNAP, good checksum values, to prove we 
--    are setup to accept a good frame.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums checked OK (bits [23:22] = 11) and SNAP (bit 24 high).
--
--  4. Check statistics for correct values from above tests.
--
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------


--******************************************************************************
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--******************************************************************************
-- Configuration Requirements ..
requires ext_fifo_interface 1
requires no_pcs 0
wait_states 0
bus_grant_delay 0


--******************************************************************************
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts
--     and then enable receive in TBI mode into a 32-bit FIFO data bus.
--******************************************************************************
-- check and initialise the relevant registers
apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register

-- this is the event count that will initialize the scaler for event counts. it will cause any future scaling to only scale
-- the counts after start_scale
start_scale

apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register
apbrd     184 00000000 -- ignore this read

apbwr     200 00000040  -- disable autonegotioation
apbrd     184 00000000 -- ignore this read


-- # Initialize the network configuration register
-- #   -eam      <1|0|random>, default = 0. This is external address matching
-- #   -duplex   <full|half|random>, default = random
-- #   -speed    <1g|100m|10m|random>, default = random
-- #   -jumbo    <1|0|random>, default = random. This wont affect the RX transactor below, but will automatically cause jumbos to be dropped.
-- #   -copy_all <1|0|random>, default = 0. If 0, ensure you initialize the dest_addr in the rx transactor to something that will match
-- #   -databus  <32|64|128|take_from_cfg|random>, default = random, bus <= config.  The max value is the value set in dma_bus_width in gem_defs.v
-- #   -rx_toe   <1|0|random>, default = 0. Enables RX TCP/IP checksum offload
-- #   -pcs_en   <1|0|random>, default = 0. Enables SGMII PCS
-- #   -pause_en <1|0|random>, default = 0. Enables pausing of transmission
-- #   -dont_copy_pause <1|0|random>, default = 0. Controls whether pause frames are copied
init_ncr -sgmii_en 0 -pcs_en 1 -retry_test 0 -copy_all 0 -duplex half -speed 1g -jumbo 0 -databus 32 -eam 0 -rx_toe 1 -pause_en 0 -dont_copy_pause 0 -multicast_hash 0 -unicast_hash 0

apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      00 00000004  -- enable receive
apbrd      00 zzzzzzzz repeat=15 -- repeat read 15 times to ensure rx enable is propagated through design

apbrd(int) 24 00000200  -- check link status change interrupt
apbwr       24 ffffffff  -- clear interrupt


